; Synthetic "internet" for the resolver check (VPR-055): what the names would resolve to without a
; policy. Addresses are from the documentation ranges (RFC 5737). A name whose answer is one of the
; 198.51.100.0/24 addresses below must never reach a client while the policy blocks it.
$ORIGIN .
$TTL 300
.                          SOA  ns.test. hostmaster.test. 1 3600 600 86400 300
.                          NS   ns.test.
; block page
block.example.org.         A    192.0.2.80
; exceptions and allowed names
wikipedia.org.             A    192.0.2.10
en.wikipedia.org.          A    192.0.2.11
khanacademy.org.           A    192.0.2.12
unlisted.example.          A    192.0.2.20
; names listed by the example policy (category feeds and local blocks)
adult-site.example.        A    198.51.100.1
bad-malware.example.       A    198.51.100.2
www.bad-malware.example.   A    198.51.100.3
c2-server.example.         A    198.51.100.4
casino-example.example.    A    198.51.100.5
fake-bank-login.example.   A    198.51.100.6
